@startuml
' UKLabsMS - shared conceptual domain model, including Sprint 2 refinements
' Multiplicities are explained in analysis.md.
title UKLabsMS - Domain Model

hide methods
hide circle
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

class Client {
    name
    citizenCardNumber
    nhsNumber
    birthDate
    sex
    taxIdentificationNumber
    phoneNumber
    email
}

class Administrator
class Receptionist
class MedicalLabTechnician
class ClinicalChemistryTechnologist
class SpecialistDoctor
class Courier

class Employee {
    ID
    name
    phoneNumber
    emailAddress
    doctorIndexNumber [0..1]
}

class Role {
    name
}

class ClinicalAnalysisLaboratory {
    code
    address
    phoneNumber
    email
    openingHour
    closingHour
}

class ChemicalLaboratory
class LabOrder

class RegisteredTest {
    dateOfPrescription
    sampleCollectionDate
}

class TestType {
    internalCode
    nhsCode
    collectionMethodDescription
}

class Parameter {
    ID
    name
    description
    metric
    metricType
}

class TestTypeParameter

class ReferenceRange {
    minimum
    maximum
}

class Sample {
    barcode
}

class ChemicalAnalysis

class ParameterResult {
    value
    recordedAt
}

class Diagnosis
class Report
class Notification

' Clients, prescriptions, tests and test definitions
Client "1" -- "0..*" LabOrder : submits >
Client "1" -- "0..*" RegisteredTest : is associated with >
Receptionist "1" -- "0..*" RegisteredTest : registers >

' Each lab order corresponds to its registered test.
LabOrder "1" -- "1" RegisteredTest : corresponds to >
RegisteredTest "0..*" -- "1" TestType : is classified as >
ClinicalAnalysisLaboratory "1" -- "0..*" RegisteredTest : collects samples for >

' TestTypeParameter is the intermediary for the many-to-many relationship.
TestType "1" -- "0..*" TestTypeParameter : defines >
TestTypeParameter "0..*" -- "1" Parameter : identifies >
' A registered test records the parameters specified in its lab order.
RegisteredTest "0..*" -- "1..*" TestTypeParameter : specifies >
Parameter "1" -- "0..1" ReferenceRange : has >

' Registered tests may exist before any sample is collected.
RegisteredTest "1" -- "0..*" Sample : has >
MedicalLabTechnician "1" -- "0..*" Sample : registers >
' Each sample is delivered by a courier.
Courier "1" -- "0..*" Sample : transports >

Sample "1" -- "0..*" ChemicalAnalysis : undergoes >
ChemicalLaboratory "1" -- "0..*" ChemicalAnalysis : hosts >
ClinicalChemistryTechnologist "1" -- "0..*" ChemicalAnalysis : performs >

ChemicalAnalysis "1" -- "1..*" ParameterResult : records >
Parameter "1" -- "0..*" ParameterResult : measured by >

RegisteredTest "1" -- "0..1" Report : results in >
Report "1" -- "1" Diagnosis : contains >
Report "0..1" -- "1..*" ParameterResult : presents >
SpecialistDoctor "1" -- "0..*" Report : prepares >

Client "1" -- "0..*" Notification : receives >
Notification "0..*" -- "1" Report : concerns >

' Management responsibility, not ownership by an individual administrator.
Administrator "0..*" -- "0..*" TestType : manages >
Administrator "0..*" -- "0..*" Parameter : manages >
Administrator "0..*" -- "0..*" ClinicalAnalysisLaboratory : manages >
Administrator "0..*" -- "0..*" Employee : manages and consults >
Employee "0..*" -- "1" Role : is assigned to >

note right of Employee
US12 and US13 share this Employee concept.
ID is numeric and sequential, starting at 1.
Phone number and e-mail address are unique.
Doctor Index Number is mandatory
when the role is Specialist Doctor.
end note

note right of Role
The accepted role catalog and its mapping
to the named professional participants
must be confirmed. No extra role values
or inheritance hierarchy are implied.
end note

note bottom of Parameter
Reference values apply only to Numeric metrics.
US11 team rule: Numeric requires a minimum
and maximum, with minimum <= maximum;
Qualitative has no numeric reference range.
end note

note bottom of TestTypeParameter
A Test Type can be registered before its
parameter associations are configured.
Use in a Registered Test requires associations
covering the prescribed parameters.
The configuration operation is not implemented.
end note

@enduml
